WEBVTT

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:31.720
<i>The seeds of worries that I thought I got 
rid of burst out my mind and sprouted</i>

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:47.950
<i>Today again, countless brambles 
spread out underfoot, awaiting me</i>

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>Where do I go in order to meet you?</i>

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:11.300
<i>Don't hold me, the thorns 
on my back will hurt you</i>

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:26.530
<i>But still, my overflowing 
emotions are searching for you</i>

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.690
"Veneer Town"

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.630
<i>It was, yes... when I was taking test 
photos with my newly obtained camera.</i>

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.880
This dark, narrow field of 
view in the viewfinder...

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.480
Cool!

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:54.660
What kind of photos are you taking?!

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:55.380
Huh?

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.470
You naughty jerk!

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.810
Naughty! Naughty!

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.230
What're you doing?

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.050
Now, if you want, I can take 
a picture of you too, Nessa.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.070
Sorry.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.530
Nessa likes having fun.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.740
Nessa also likes watching 
everyone having fun.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.910
Say, are you having fun right now, Clain?

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.710
I guess... Yeah.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.700
Then, Nessa is having fun, too.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.510
<i>So said Nessa, smiling...</i>

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:43.140
<i>although I didn't know at that time what 
feelings she had within that smile...</i>

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.560
Good morning.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:55.980
Did you have a nice dream?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.600
Welcome to Xanadu, the perfect city.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.500
What do you think?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.300
Wh... Wh-Wh-Wh...

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:20.760
Wh-Wh...?

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.180
Who are you?!

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.140
You don't remember?

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:27.080
After we spent such a 
passionate evening together?

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.770
D-Don't tell me I...

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:31.660
Oh, watch out over there.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.190
So you weren't aware after all.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:38.280
The bed and the sheet you 
have are solid objects.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:41.180
But the decoration on the 
bed is an air object.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.690
So are the carpet and paintings.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.200
What replication capabilities...!

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.580
To think that it can process 
such an expansive reality...

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.540
I told you... that this 
is a perfect city, right?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:56.290
This is the only city in the world where 
Fractale is still perfectly functioning.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.680
Perfectly? Then, don't tell me...

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:01.800
I'm Megan.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.550
Then, you too... Ms. Megan?

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:07.000
Of course, I'm a doppel, too. See?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.470
Amazing!

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.040
Thanks. So don't worry.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:16.560
Unfortunately, I haven't even laid 
a finger on you, loincloth boy.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.440
My name is Clain!

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.360
So why am I...

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.200
You were lying on the street 
at the edge of the town.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.570
<i>That's right! Last night...</i>

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.120
Say... There's plenty of water here.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.950
Why can't we use this water?

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:35.000
This is a salt-water lake, so 
this water isn't for drinking.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.500
What a waste, that you 
can't use all this water.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.760
But if we can find a river 
flowing into this lake,

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.600
it should definitely be fresh water.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.840
So, let's keep at it a little longer. Okay?

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:47.640
Of course!

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:52.100
Nessa is having fun because 
Nessa is with Clain!

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.190
Clain and Phryne are the only 
ones Nessa feels warm around.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.860
But Phryne gets upset 
when Nessa clings to her.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:01.650
That's why you...

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.500
cling to you!

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.660
Maybe Phryne and the others or 
someone else is talking about you.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.340
Nessa?

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.920
Nessa feels kind of strange...

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:24.590
Nessa's head isn't working. 
Nessa feels dizzy...

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.020
What happened?! It's out of control!

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.560
What the heck?! What happened?!

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.370
I didn't find him around here.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:54.970
Which suggests that at least he 
didn't die in the crash, huh?

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.580
Then, I wonder where Clain went...

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.250
Miss...

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.800
It's a beautiful day, isn't it?

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:12.470
Wow...

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.580
So this is... the perfect city...

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.540
Amazing, isn't it?

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:24.110
I was impressed when I came 
here for the first time.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.570
Are you an idiot? The number 
of balloons is going down.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:29.470
I never want to take the form 
of a shabby, ugly doppel again.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:35.660
Forget that... Why do I 
have to dress like this?

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:39.540
Because you stand out in a bad 
way since you are a real body.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.830
When in Rome, do as the Romans do.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:44.710
When in Xanadu, do things 
the Xanadu way. Okay?

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.640
<i>If those people could come 
to a town like this...</i>

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.940
<i>I bet they would've been happy.</i>

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.740
<i>Nessa should be back at the Danan, right?</i>

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.700
<i>She seemed kinda sick...</i>

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.910
What? You like that kind of stuff?

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.870
You have bad taste.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.490
It's not like I like this stuff.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:20.230
If you want to enjoy art, 
check out my works.

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:22.830
They are a lot better than that.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:23.630
Your works?

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:26.630
I'm a sculptress.

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:31.470
One of my works once was in the top 100 
in the air sculpture download store.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:36.020
I'm sorry. I don't know much 
about that kind of stuff...

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:42.620
Well, you don't even use a doppel in this 
day and age so you can't help it, huh?

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:47.230
But you can't tell how amazing this 
city is when you are a real body.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:51.450
In this city, you can find all the 
culture, art and entertainment...

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.030
as well as the wealth and all the 
information to support those things.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.540
If you desire, you can 
experience them all...

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.660
everything in the world...

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:04.120
Or, would you prefer to experience these?

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:04.830
Sorry!

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.170
Then, let's go back home.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.920
I can get all sorts of data 
drugs, so we can have some fun.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.510
N-No thanks!

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:15.430
Actually, I have a companion and 
I-I'm worried about her, so...

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.300
Your companion?

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.550
Her name is Nessa.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:22.890
Oh, I'm so worried. I wonder where she went.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:27.940
Nessa...?!

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:31.740
I see. You must be worried.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:35.480
My friends are scattered around this valley.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:36.910
I'll ask them.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.160
Thank you very much.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.830
By the way, what's this village?

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.960
Could it be that you're part 
of the Lost Millennium?

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:50.180
It's nothing scary like that.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:56.970
In this village, we all live as one 
with nature, appreciating its blessing.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:01.180
It's a community of people who 
share the same ideals, so to speak.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:06.900
Wow...! This is kinda amazing!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.320
This is lovely! Don't you think, Phryne?!

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.960
Is that right?

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:21.540
Are you really sure this is the place?

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.830
Yeah, I recognized that room.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.000
You can say that he's one of 
my artist friends, I guess.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.130
The resident here is a doppel designer.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:34.180
He designs one-off bodies, 
not multi-purpose ones.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:37.380
An air object?

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:50.010
Colin! It's me! Megan!

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:52.220
Stop these stupid guards!

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.700
Oh? Someone I haven't seen in a while 
brought a guest you don't see often...

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.710
I wonder how long it's been since 
a real human came to visit me here.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:11.500
U-Uhm... Isn't there a girl doppel 
who looks about 10 years old here?

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:15.170
Oh? What's your relationship to her?

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:17.260
Ah...! So she's here?!

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.380
I'm the one who's asking a question.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:22.460
I'm... well... her...

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:24.640
<i>What am I to her?</i>

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:26.730
Never mind.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.160
Come in.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.820
Nessa!

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.500
Nessa! It's me, Clain! Nessa!

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:44.530
Ah... Clain... Good...

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.750
Nessa! Hang in there!

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:50.210
You're warm! You have a fever, Nessa!

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.380
Oh?

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:54.800
So she can even send a tactile emulation 
signal to a real human, huh?

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.430
She might be <i>the real deal</i>.

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:58.050
What'd you do to her?!

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.380
Why is Nessa...

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:00.740
Calm down.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:03.930
All I did was take her in when 
I found her lying on the street.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:07.360
She's probably come down with a virus.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:08.350
Virus...

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.690
Or, maybe she's being hacked.

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:15.650
Whatever it is, she's unconsciously 
fighting back what's trying to attack her.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.820
White blood cells fight viruses 
that entered your body

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.240
even if you're unaware of it, right?

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.430
When that happens, humans run a fever.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:25.530
This is like that.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:29.760
With her latent specs, she should 
be able to engineer the attack

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:33.380
and turn the intruder 
into the victim instead.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.920
But it seems she either can't 
do it or doesn't know how.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.720
Nessa's sorry, Clain.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:45.470
Nessa came out to find someone 
who could help us, but...

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.430
That's okay, Nessa.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.160
You still haven't been able to break through?

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.820
I'm sorry.

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:07.130
It has a thick barrier 
and it's quick to escape.

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:08.490
Keep chasing it.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:12.620
We finally got a lead. Don't let it go.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.340
Yes, Sir.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.520
Sir Barrot, there was a 
response to the search notice.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:25.140
Get Odin ready for takeoff.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:27.680
Really?

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:28.600
Yep.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:31.420
Hide-and-seek and tag, too?

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:33.810
High-up tag and hopscotch, as well?!

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.610
I'll even do "tasty" dancing for you, too.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.120
So get well soon.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:42.320
Pinky swear!

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:43.950
Pinky swear?

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.860
Sanko taught Nessa.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:47.280
It's a sign of a promise.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:49.820
Give Nessa your pinky finger, too, Clain!

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:51.290
Like this?

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.040
If you break your promise, you'll have 
to swallow a thousand needles, okay?

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.170
Boy, that would be a problem.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:05.460
If you break your promise, you'll 
have to swallow a thousand needles!

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:03.130
It's those kids, right?

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:06.880
The ones the temple put out a reward for?

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:08.640
Oh, so you knew?

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:12.930
Yeah. Fortunately, we're the only 
ones who've noticed, though.

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.680
Say, I have a favor to ask.

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:18.060
Would you let me take the credit?

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:21.110
I'm having a bit of a hard time right now.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.490
As it stands, it looks 
like I'll have to give up

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:26.280
the right to use the network circuit. So...

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:28.620
Then you should leave this town.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.490
Those who can't earn monay can 
cling to donay and take it easy.

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.960
That'd be living within your means, right?

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.040
I-I'm working on a plan for my next piece!

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:41.840
Once it's completed, I'm sure 
those who pose as net critics

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.880
will throw themselves at my feet!

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:45.200
So...

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.590
Please...?

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:50.800
How disgusting.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:53.250
You took the trouble to counter those

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.710
who criticized your work, and 
ended up causing a flame war.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.440
Don't you remember your real world 
identity was revealed because of that?

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.820
Then let's think about the share later.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.400
To tell you the truth, I've 
already contacted the temple.

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:11.740
So if we can keep them here for 
just a little bit longer...

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:16.790
But isn't the temple also after one 
more person, a human girl, too?

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:18.710
If we don't give them together, the 
reward amount will drop, right?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.920
There's no need to worry about that.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:27.720
Darn it...

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:32.390
There's no information at all on them 
in the past 24 hours on the net.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:34.680
I see. That's worrisome.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:37.730
Hey, Phryne...

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:41.310
You and Clain... Well... What's the deal?

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.270
"What's the deal?" What're you talking about?

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:46.900
Well... how should I say... 
how should I put it...

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:50.910
I-I-In other words, how far 
are you on your relationship?

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:52.620
Huh...?

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.120
Miss Innocent Chop!

00:14:56.430 --> 00:15:00.370
I'm talking about your 
relationship... or dating...

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:03.340
In other words, I'm asking if you two 
are having a naughty relationship!

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:06.020
Oh, I see...

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:06.900
So...?

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.260
Clain is a friend.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:11.380
Is that right?

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:17.640
Yes... because I don't deserve 
to be liked by someone.

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:18.700
Huh?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.680
Miss! Got a minute?

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:24.770
What is it?

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:45.130
Oh? Did you have some business at my atelier?

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:48.020
No, not really. I'm sorry.

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:50.090
That's no problem. More importantly,

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:53.620
what's your impression? What 
do you think of my work?

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.890
It's... interesting.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.970
Oh, intriguing?

00:15:57.970 --> 00:15:59.560
Yes, very much.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.020
It somehow looks like a nerve-wrecked 
earthworm is tap-dancing.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.860
I see.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:09.650
So you're like those ignorant 
people who pose as critics, huh?

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:10.570
Huh?

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:16.740
You damn worm! You don't even have the 
intelligence to understand my art!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.700
You're a damn scum who nests on the net!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:33.010
Oh? You've suddenly become obedient.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.520
This is good.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.600
Die!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.180
You're beyond naughty! You damn evil villain!

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.740
Are you all right, Phryne?

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:47.440
En... ri...

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:48.880
Pull yourself together!

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:51.600
The people here are outrageous liars!

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:52.150
What?

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:56.780
We heard that most of the people in 
this valley are residents of Xanadu.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:57.770
Xanadu?

00:16:57.770 --> 00:17:00.910
It's a city where the Fractale 
System is still perfectly alive...

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:03.870
A city where only those who are 
earning tons of monay can live.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.250
Then the people in this village are...

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.880
billionaires who are utterly 
steeped in Fractale.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.010
They put their doppels in 
town and make them work.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:16.220
And then, they, the real humans, 
are playing naturalist nomads.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:19.760
And, one of those loaded people said

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:23.960
that it seemed that Gail guy 
took in a boy last night.

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:24.430
What?

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:43.910
Ow!

00:17:52.310 --> 00:17:54.630
Dammit! That damn bitch!

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.430
That brat...! Dammit!

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.940
Does it hurt? Are you okay, Clain?

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.830
You're warm, Nessa.

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:12.190
Clain?

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:15.160
To tell you the truth,

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:18.660
there's something I realized 
after coming to a city like this.

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:25.500
Well... being in the world where you 
can't touch things is very lonesome...

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.120
and cold... So I noticed.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:31.150
I'm sorry that I didn't notice it until now.

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:34.230
Clain!

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.600
I won't let you escape!

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:51.660
That's a virus worm that interferes 
with the terminal inside your body!

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:59.150
Stop it!

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:02.470
No...

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:06.980
Nessa will... protect...

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.040
Nessa will protect Clain!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.180
This is...

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:06.040
Is this really... Xanadu?!

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:08.980
Miss, look over at 2 o'clock...

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.560
Good... Clain...

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:20.490
Nessa... Did you do this?

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:23.860
Don't come close!

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:28.620
That's no use.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:31.160
This droid is running stand-alone.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:34.580
Your power is really amazing.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:38.750
The rumor about the "key" that can 
save Fractale or destroy it...

00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:41.100
That's about you, isn't it?

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.140
But I can't allow it...

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:46.470
Fractale means everything to me.

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:50.930
There're people who can be 
free only within this world.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.680
I'll never let it end.

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:02.360
Nooooooo!

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:05.520
Clain!

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:10.400
Clain!

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:17.330
Oh? There you are.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:23.510
I've looked all over for 
you, my sweet tomboy.

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:37.480
<i>The same sleepy winter afternoon 
is repeated every day</i>

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:51.930
<i>Just once, I had a dream that 
I slipped off of a salley tree</i>

00:21:52.660 --> 00:22:06.210
<i>Until the warmth you left 
behind becomes light</i>

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:20.200
<i>I will picture you in the sunny spot 
that I've grown accustomed to going to</i>

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:48.510
<i>The sunny spot that strokes 
my cheek reminds me of you</i>
